cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite these texts, cite the release of this repository you used (its
  version, and its DOI when one is given) and the printed PTS edition (volume
  and page). corrections.json changes between releases; the corrections are
  recorded there with their sources.
type: dataset
title: "pts-gretil-ng: PTS Pali texts from GRETIL, proofread"
abstract: >-
  The Pali canon (Tipitaka) in the printed editions of the Pali Text Society
  (PTS), as given by GRETIL, the Göttingen Register of Electronic Texts in
  Indian Languages (digital input by the Dhammakaya Foundation): 44 HTML files,
  43 volumes, readable in a browser at https://jorgecaa.github.io/pts-gretil-ng/.
  Where GRETIL departs from the printed edition, the text was proofread against
  scans of the printed volumes and the printed reading is restored and marked.
  Corrections of the editions themselves published by the PTS (M. Cone's
  Dictionary of Pāli, P. Jackson's revision of Saṃyutta IV, W. Pruitt's
  correction lists, the corrigenda printed in the volumes) are applied and
  marked, with the printed reading they replace. The build is reproducible
  from a pinned commit of the GRETIL mirror; every correction is recorded with
  its source in corrections.json.
